\f1\i Most have Never Stirred\ulnone \
We are going to die\
That is what we must face\
We are the lucky ones\
Most never join the race.\
Never will they perish\
Never to falter and fall\
Owning no life to cherish\
They were never born at all.\
The number of human beings\
Who could be here in my place,\
Outnumber all the sand grains\
On the Sahara\'92s sandy face.\
Untold unborn poets rhyming better than Keats\
Countless bright minds Newton could not resist\
The set of potential people and their possible feats\
Exceeds the set of human beings that ever will exist.\
In the teeth of these odds stupefying\
You and I living banal and trite\
Are the privileged few, there is no denying\
Winning a grand lottery to breathe air here tonight.\
How dare we find ourselves whining,\
At the prospect of being interred\
Returning to the prior state\
From which most have never stirred.
